From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 03:23:50 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] power: coordinate MSM8660 collapse, wake and hotplug

Keep the Scorpion CPU, SAW, clocks, AVS, RPMRS and PM8058 suspend
integration together. Select the Sony/Fuji eight-level RPMRS table from real sleep votes,
latency constraints, RTC deadline and wake detectability. Preserve
RPM-notified collapse, standalone collapse and WFI fallback.

Adapt the maintained MPM irqchip to Sony MSM8660 message-RAM layout,
IPC ordering, GPIO wake routing and edge replay. Coordinate MPM with
RPMRS for PXO OFF/VDD retention profiles, including rollback. Use native MPM wake routes for PXO OFF and retention.

Gate CPU1 warm entry on a fresh secondary release and re-enable only
the wake SGI after ARM tears down per-CPU IPIs for hotplug.

Mask inherited APPS GPIO interrupt forwarding before the receiving
kernel enables the TLMM summary IRQ after kexec. Preserve pending
status and modem/direct-connect routing.

Mask and acknowledge unmapped pending PM8xxx sources inherited from
the previous kernel so their level parent cannot starve child probing.

Reinitialize MDP4 fetch/CSC/port state and interrupt enables after noirq
power loss, before restoring the atomic display state. Keep prepare-only
aborts on the ordinary complete path.

Keep platform suspend available with cpuidle.off=1 so automatic idle and
explicit system sleep can be validated independently. Debug messages report
RPMRS, clock and collapse results through dynamic debug only.

Provide PM8xxx irq_mask, as in Sony, so MASK_ON_SUSPEND actually closes
non-wake sources without clearing pending events. mask_ack alone is not
called by the generic suspend mask path.

Consume RPM polling acknowledgments in Sony order: wait for the GIC ACK
edge, read/clear message RAM, flush the clear, then clear the consumed
pending edge. A stale ACK must not abort the subsequent CPU WFI.

Order MPU3050 auxiliary-bus suspend/resume after the gate and balance
runtime references only for successful mux selects. Preserve asynchronous
PM and normal autosuspend.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---

